comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T06:48:41.698Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1711 Codex review (P2), fixed in this PR. The runtime guide catalogue in src/sdk/guide-topics.ts still listed docs/RELEASING.md as a required document of the release topic, so on an npm install pm guide release at standard or deep depth would warn 'Missing required guide document: docs/RELEASING.md'. The same topic already listed scripts/release/run-gates.mjs, which the package never shipped, so that warning predated this change. Both entries are now optional and say they exist only in a repository checkout. The docs-skills gate could not see the gap because it runs guides from the checkout. It now also applies package.json files in npm order (isPackagedPath) and fails when a required guide document is not shipped (validateGuideDocsPackaged); the spec covers a negated pattern, a dot-directory and the real repository.\n"
